# local-seo-agent

Local SEO is finicky. Google Business Profile, citation building, geogrid tracking, review management — each has its own tool and cadence. This agent ties them into one autonomous run.

## What it does

1. **GBP health check.** Pulls profile state (info accuracy, photo count, recent posts, Q&A, review velocity) via the official Google Business Profile API. NOT via Chrome automation of the GBP UI — Google's ToS prohibits automated UI access.
2. **Heat-map / geogrid run.** Triggers your geogrid tool (Localo, Local Falcon, etc.) via their official APIs.
3. **Citation audit.** Checks NAP consistency across citation sources you have official API access to (Yext, BrightLocal, etc.) or licensed data providers. Don't scrape citation sites that prohibit automation.
4. **Review monitoring.** Flags new reviews (5★, 1★, content needing response) via the GBP API reviews endpoint.
5. **Posts to your team channel.** Per-client snapshot — wins, risks, action items.

## Why it works

Local SEO has more moving parts than national. Without an aggregator, account managers track 5 tools per client. This compresses to one report per client.

## Important: timing

Run during US business hours (or your client's business hours). Local SEO tools — and Google itself — apply different heuristics overnight. Heat-map runs at 3am can artificially depress visibility scores because real users aren't searching at that time. Schedule for ~3pm GMT (mid-day US Eastern) for US-targeted clients.

## What you provide

- Google Business Profile API access (OAuth flow, business locations linked).
- Geogrid tool API (Localo, Local Falcon, GeoRanker).
- Citation source list per client (with API access where available).
- Team channel.

## Architectural considerations

- **NAP consistency is binary.** Either all citations match or they don't. Don't grade — flag the mismatches.
- **Review responses need humans.** The agent flags; humans respond. Auto-responding to negative reviews is a guaranteed PR fire.
- **Geogrids cost.** Each geogrid run is real money. Cap to weekly per client unless something's actively changing.
- **Photos matter more than people think.** GBP profiles with fresh photos this month outrank those that haven't been touched in 6 months. Track photo recency.

## What this skill does NOT include

- Auto-responding to reviews.
- Auto-modifying GBP (high-risk; humans only).
- Citation building scripts that hit non-public APIs (many violate ToS).

